{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>But if YHWH creates a creation</b> – Ibn Ezra wrote (on Numbers 16:30): There are those who say that <i>beriah</i> (creation) denotes bringing something into being from nothing, yet many lands have already split open and dwellings descended into them into the depth. But its meaning is like <i>gezirah</i> (decree), from <b>“and He will create (וּבָרֵא) them”</b> (Ezekiel 23:47). But the correct view is that it is said of the bringing of a thing into being from nothing, for in the Holy Tongue we have no term that indicates this other than this word. However, the matter is that the splitting of the ground is not a new <i>beriah</i>, but the opening of the earth's mouth to swallow is a novelty that never was from eternity, for when the ground splits as has happened many times in the earthquake called <i>zalzalah</i>, it remains open, and also the fissure fills with water and becomes like pools. But that it should open and close immediately like a man who opens his mouth to swallow and closes it after swallowing — this thing was newly brought into being on that day as though it were created from nothing. And this is the meaning of <b>“and the earth covered them”</b> (Numbers 16:33), and therefore Scripture said after <b>“and the ground split”</b> (Numbers 16:31), <b>“and the earth opened its mouth and swallowed them”</b> (Numbers 16:32). And according to the opinion of our Sages (Sanhedrin 110a), that nearby the opening of Gehinnom was also newly brought into being for that hour:"], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {0 "Reading וְיָרְדוּ הַדָּרִים (\"and dwellings descended\") with the text as given; the phrase is unusual but rendered literally."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:06:25.172051932Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}